  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid Rhapsido (remibrutinib), a BTK inhibitor / kinase inhibitor, effective 2026-03-01. Approval criteria and concomitant biologic denial encoded; supporting clinical documentation requires manual review.",
    "Cautions (notes only): increased risk of mucocutaneous-related bleeding; concomitant antithrombotic agents may further increase risk. Avoid strong CYP3A4 inhibitors or inducers. Common adverse reactions include nasopharyngitis, bleeding, headache, nausea and abdominal pain.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization up to 1 year. Manual review required.",
    "Quantity (notes only): 60 tablets per 30 days. Manual review required."
